  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 243 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nUpper high pressure over Hudson Bay combined with upper high \npressure over the Four Corners region, will lead to progressive \nwesterly flow over much of the northern CONUS with periodic \nembedded short waves passing across Iowa. This flow will also \nkeep a surface boundary in the Midwest area and resulting in \nseveral chances for thunderstorms before Canadian high pressure \narrives early next week. PWAT values of 1.50-2.00\" will be \ncommon during active storm periods that could lead to an \naggregate heavy rain threat through the week. Temperatures will \nbe seasonal and mainly in the 80s through midweek the gradual \ncooling as the Canadian high pressure approaches for the end of \nnext week.",
